**Last Updated: August 4TH 2026**

### Summary 
This dataset repository contains de-identified fMRI and T1-weighted imaging data acquired from 10  Parkinson's disease patients (aged 50-76 years) receiving deep brain stimulation therapy. All patients were implanted in either the Subthalamic Nucleus or the Globus Pallidus Internus.

### Data Acquisition
For details on data acquisition, please refer to the attached JSON files below.

### BOLD Metadata

Two BOLD JSON sidecar files are provided to account for differences in the number of slices across subjects.

| Subjects | Number of slices (`dim3`) | `SliceTiming` values |
|----------|--------------------------:|---------------------:|
| `sub-01`, `sub-16` | 36 | 36 |
| `sub-02`, `sub-03`, `sub-04`, `sub-05`, `sub-06`, `sub-12`, `sub-13`, `sub-14` | 38 | 38 |

Use the BOLD JSON sidecar with the corresponding number of `SliceTiming` values for each subject.

### Study Details
For information on our test-retest study and subsequent findings, please refer to our manuscript: 
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nicl.2026.103973

